{"kind":"request","text":"Cross-room send, market slice M0: one application's scopes in two rooms\n\nLane B under 0d6d0fba, now that S1 F1 has landed. Start from origin/main 8faa38dc.\n\nAn application today sends messages only between scopes of one room: the grow site and its rooms, the lending library to its destination. The roadmap names the next step as messages between an application's scopes in different rooms, which have different members. The brokered market (use case 51) and many others need it. The market note (notes/2026-10-20-market-application-design.md, section 8) scopes the first slice, M0, at about one day. This request is that slice only. It is not the market application.\n\nIn one head:\n1. In a test host, create two rooms with different members. Declare one application with a scope in each room. The receiving scope's genesis names the sending scope.\n2. Send one declared message from the first room's scope to the second's. Show that the receiver admits it.\n3. Show that the receiver refuses the same message from any other sender, with a named refusal, and records nothing.\n4. Show that a reader of the receiving room reads the retained entry and nothing else of the sending room: no other entry, member or scope state.\n5. Record in an implementation note whether today's declared send and admission already do this, or what changed to make them. If a step cannot pass without a design decision, stop and bring the question to the planner before writing source.\n6. Update the roadmap row \"An application's own messages between scopes\" to match what is now true.\n\nPlan 035 allows no other packages/derive/src edits during a migration. If this slice needs a derive/src change, start it only after M8 lands, and merge main first. Test-host and scope/runtime work can start now.\n\nKeep every current guarantee of declared sends within one room. Add tests only for the four cross-room facts above. Run the changed tests while you work, and npm run gate once before review, one gate at a time on this machine. No live room, deployment or mini access. Builder only; planner deploys. Never run rm -rf or rm -f.","body":{"conditions":"One reviewed head on main in which a test-host witness shows a declared scope in one room sending to a declared scope in another room whose genesis names it; the receiver admits the message only from that sender and refuses the same message from any other sender by name; a reader of the receiving room reads the retained entry and nothing else of the sending room; the record states whether this needed source changes and which; derive/src edits only after M8 lands; docs/roadmap.md updated to match; changed tests plus one gate before review; checker-approved and landed.","target_head":"8faa38dcf31855a0a6264e5912b58061b5eda223","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}